                <pb facs="0365" n="349" sameAs="frus:frus1950v01/pg349"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>United States–United Kingdom political-military conversations occurred in
                    Washington during July 20–24, 1950. The United States was represented in the
                    discussions by General Omar N. Bradley, Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff,
                    and Ambassador at Large Philip C. Jessup. British representatives were Sir
                    Oliver Franks, British Ambassador to the United States, and Marshal of the Royal
                    Air Force Lord Tedder, Chairman of the British Joint Services Mission. The
                    primary subject of consideration was the world situation in light of the
                    outbreak of the Korean War. For documentation on these conversations, see <ref
                        target="frus:frus1950v03/pg_1654">volume III, pages 1654</ref> ff.</p>
            </div>
